    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d120">

                <pb facs="0277" n="153" sameAs="frus:frus1921v01/pg153"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">813.00/1061</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Honduras</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Spencer</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tegucigalpa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-02-15"><hi rendition="#italic">February 15,
                        1921</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received March 3.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 70</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to enclose copy with
                    translation of a Foreign Office note, received today,<anchor n="30"
                        xml:id="d120-f1"/> in which I am informed that the Covenant of the Central
                    American Federation has been approved by the President and ratified by the
                    National Congress. The dates of the above ceremonies are given in detail in the
                    two enclosed notes.<anchor n="30" xml:id="d120-f2"/></p>
                <p>I have the honor also to enclose copies of the Official Gazette under date of
                    February 15, last [<hi rendition="#italic">1921</hi>],<anchor n="30"
                        xml:id="d120-f3"/> in which the minute details and terms of the treaty are
                    set forth.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Willing Spencer</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
